1
00:00:00,643 --> 00:00:03,983
(Leonard:)For the same reason I don't
wear the apron or the hair net.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,910
(Sheldon:)Fine. What about epilepsy?

3
00:00:06,916 --> 00:00:08,746
(Leonard:)I don't have epilepsy, either.

4
00:00:08,751 --> 00:00:11,251
(Sheldon:)You don't,
but the surgeon might, hmm?

5
00:00:11,254 --> 00:00:14,584
(Sheldon:)And your carotid artery is just
one shaky scalpel away

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:18,260
(Sheldon:)from becoming the dancing
fountain at Disneyland.

7
00:00:18,261 --> 00:00:21,761
(Leonard:)Sheldon, do you realize that
driving is riskier than surgery?

8
00:00:21,764 --> 00:00:24,804
(Sheldon:)I do. I have the drive
to the hospital right here.

9
00:00:24,801 --> 00:00:26,171
(Sheldon:)That is if
you make it

10
00:00:26,169 --> 00:00:28,969
(Sheldon:)to the car without
falling down the stairs.

11
00:00:28,971 --> 00:00:31,841
(Sheldon:)And don't expect me to carry
you, I do that enough in life.

12
00:00:33,142 --> 00:00:34,942
Buddy, I-I get that
you're worried about me

13
00:00:34,944 --> 00:00:37,814
and I-I appreciate that,
but I'm not going to die.

14
00:00:37,814 --> 00:00:39,614
(Sheldon:)You don't know that.
Well...

15
00:00:39,615 --> 00:00:42,755
(Leonard:)I do know that it won't
be from an asteroid strike.

16
00:00:44,287 --> 00:00:45,787
(Sheldon:)You know who else said that?

17
00:00:45,788 --> 00:00:47,688
(Sheldon:)Every cocky T. rex
currently swimming around

18
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:49,860
(Sheldon:)in the gas tank of your car.

19
00:00:50,793 --> 00:00:52,663
I-If there was
an asteroid strike,

20
00:00:52,662 --> 00:00:53,792
(Leonard:)wouldn't you die, too?

21
00:00:53,796 --> 00:00:55,526
(Sheldon:)I don't know--
I'm smart and scrappy,

22
00:00:55,531 --> 00:00:59,021
(Sheldon:)I think I'd find a way.

